RESULTS DAY TO REMEMBER! 🎓 🥳 What a fantastic day! A huge congratulations to all of our incredible Year 11 students on an out of this world day of results. The hard work, determination, and resilience have really paid off! 🥳 Everyone at TBCC could not be more proud of every single one of you. With a huge thank you to our brilliant staff, supportive families, and everyone else who has made these achievements possible. ❤️ We look forward to supporting the next stage in your life, whatever it is that comes next for you. 🏆 #gcseresults #resultsday #classof2026 #year11
@thomasbennett.communitycollege
🎓✨️ A-Level RESULTS DAY 2026 A massive congratulations to all of our wonderful A-Level students on the results they received today! We are incredibly proud of what you have achieved, as well as the resilience and hard work you have brought with you to get over the finish line! This has been a remarkable year for your grades! However your future unfolds, Thomas Bennett wishes you every success whilst you take the next stage in reaching the best versions of yourselves. 💙💛 #ResultsDay #ALevelResults #Classof2026 #NextSteps
@thomasbennett.communitycollege
Last week, Ms Wilson attended the Royal Garden Party at Buckingham Palace in recognition of her outstanding contribution to education after more than 25 years at Thomas Bennett. Accompanied by Vegas, her Hearing Dog, she had the honour of meeting King Charles, Queen Camilla and The Princess Royal with the pair becoming stars of the event and featuring across national media! Ms Wilson continues to be a passionate advocate for disability awareness, especially invisible disabilities, proving that nothing should stand in the way of achieving your dreams. Congratulations Ms Wilson and Vegas! 👏✨ #tbcc
